      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why aren\u0027t all the accesses to the tcpcs serialized through a single task? How is one supposed to maintain correct tcpc state when there are multiple tasks at play who can directly affect the tcpc state -- which can make the hardware state and the software maintained state be different.\n\nThe current construction of this change relies on there not being a race in the hook task with higher priority tasks? This may make the problem harder to trigger, but I think I\u0027m missing how it\u0027s completely prevented.",
      "revId": "ec7841e40446c2754549d8d68ac1fc9a742cea8a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a47329de_e51af1cb",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-08T23:08:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This CL ensures that there are no deterministic events that that can result in the low power entry/exit cycle repeating forever. It also improves the likelihood that TCPC accesses won\u0027t happen while it\u0027s in low power mode and therefore will NAK a request attempt. I don\u0027t think this is relying on there not being a race condition between hooks and higher priority tasks. There may still be some instance of going into low power mode, then having another TCPC access attempt  undo that, but if nothing is attached, the USB PD state machine will always request entry into low power mode again.\n\nPrior to this CL and the previous one that refactors tcpc_alert(), there were TCPC accesses by lower priority tasks that were always generated in conjunction with events (coming out of reset, chipset power state change, or cable detach events) such as processing TCPC alerts and checking VBUS level (via TCPC) that precipitated the enter/exit cycle. The parade TCPC does NAK TCPC request attempts when in low power mode, but unlike the ANX7447 doesn\u0027t appear to use that as a trigger to wake from low power mode and drive the alert line to the EC. So that\u0027s why the ANX7447 exposed this design issue w.r.t low power mode.",
      "parentUuid": "fd045a82_adc77b8b",
      "revId": "ec7841e40446c2754549d8d68ac1fc9a742cea8a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
