      "writtenOn": "2018-05-08T23:08:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the bit that\u0027s about to be cleared (which just means that the TCPC for a port has a low power mode entry pending), gets set while the tcpc_write() function is happening, then that\u0027s really just a duplicate request to enter low power mode. The \u0027enter low power mode\u0027 request only comes from the PD task and so that can run when the hook task gives up control waiting for the TCPC access to complete, but that\u0027s not new information and should be ignored.",
      "parentUuid": "71194ab7_814b2b98",
      "revId": "ec7841e40446c2754549d8d68ac1fc9a742cea8a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
